  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason : This is required by Section of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) (England) Regulations 2007 (as amended).\r",
    "The approved development shall be carried out in accordance with the following drawings/ details :\rLocation Plan\rSite Location Plan Project No 100-NDLA-00-00-DR-L\rProposed Hoarding and  Advert Plan, Drawing No MG-ADC-001\rProposed Banner Details, Drawing No MG_ADC-003\rProposed Hoarding and Banners Elevation, Drawing No MG_ADC_002\rHoarding Banners, Drawing No MG_ADC_004 Rev 00\rHoarding Banners, Drawing No MG_ADC_005 Rev 00\r\rReason : For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "No advertisement is to be displayed without the permission of the owner of the site or any other person with an interest in the site entitled to grant permission.\r\rReason : This is required by Regulation 14 of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) (England) Regulations 2007(as amended)\r\r",
    "No advertisement shall be sited or displayed so as to : endanger persons using any highway, railway,waterway, dock, harbour or aerodrome (civil or military); obscure, or hinder the ready interpretation of, any  traffic sign, railway signal or aid to navigation by water or air; or hinder the operation of any device used for the purpose of security or surveillance or for measuring the speed of any vehicle. \r\rReason : This is required by Regulation 14 of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) (England) Regulations 2007(as amended)\r",
    "Any advertisement displayed,and any site used for display of advertisements, shall be maintained in a condition that does not impact the visual amenity of the site.\r\rReason : This is required by Regulation 14 of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) (England) Regulations 2007 (as amended).\r",
    "Any structure or hoarding erected or used principally for the purpose of displaying advertisements shall be maintained in a condition that does not endanger the public.\r\rReason : This is required by Regulation 14 of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) (England) Regulations 2007 (as amended).\r\r",
    "Where an advertisement is required under these Regulations to be removed, the site shall be left in a condition that does not endanger the public or impair visual amenity.\r\rReason : This is required by Regulation 14 of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) (England) Regulations 2007(as amended)\r"
  ],
